{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/583012-vampire-hunter-crossover-game","id":583012,"title":"Vampire-Hunter crossover game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-07T19:14:55-07:00","id":583012,"title":"Vampire-Hunter crossover game","content":"Hi there,<br /> <br /> I was hoping to hear some thoughts and discussion regarding a Hunter game and its compatibility with a cWoD vampire game. Technically it looks like Hunter is in the nWoD and is dealing with vampires from that world and I haven't touched VtR. <br /> <br /> First - assuming its possible, what does it look like to storytell a game with mortal hunter players and kindred players? Is it near impossible to balance and leave all players satisfied, or does it generally even itself out?<br /> Second - how problematic (if at all) would it be to remain in the VtM world, complete with its sects, clans and histories, and involve lore and backstories from Hunter (i.e. do they directly conflict in any obvious predictable ways).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6101-talltales","name":"talltales","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T19:33:46-07:00","id":583068,"title":"","content":"If you're doing VtM, why not use Hunters Hunted? It's actually built for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T19:51:25-07:00","id":583088,"title":"","content":"The power difference between Hunter: the Vigil characters and Kindred, whether using cWoD or nWoD systems for the latter, is stark. Vigil is unique among the WoD games in that it is a big title gameline which doesn't really have a &quot;monster template.&quot; A hunter differs so little from a blue-book civilian mortal that they're often not really metaphysically distinguishable. Injuries are harder to prevent and last longer. There's no True Faith to &quot;level the playing field.&quot; And, of course, there's the usual problem with Vampire crossovers, where half the party is nocturnal and the other is not.<br /> <br /> If you can handle issues like that, though (possibly by running two parallel groups of players in linked games \u2014 although I'd be wary of running it adversarially rather than having some common enemies and cautious tensions), there's little to nothing about Hunter: the Vigil that prevents it from coexisting with the world of Vampire: the Masquerade. There's a conspiratorial Shadow Congregation within the Catholic Church that is similar but a little different from VtM's modern Inquisition, and nWoD in general is presented with a tone implying less direct monstrous influence over mortal politics and power structures, but Hunter makes very few overt setting statements about the supernatural, and those which it does fit pretty comfortably along the edges of the cWoD overall. Not only do hunters generally not know a huge amount about the night-to-night unlives and motives of the monsters they hunt, but Vigil generally assumes that the corresponding WoD gamelines aren't a comprehensive guide to what it is they're fighting. Any lore from Vampire: the Requiem is kept behind a layer of obfuscation and ambiguity, and extra lore is dropped that intentionally doesn't fit, other types of blood-drinking monsters that are not Kindred and don't show up in Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T17:52:01-07:00","id":585484,"title":"","content":"For what it is worth, in a long hunter game I was in, we murdered a number of Broujha (and were murdered by some in turn)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}